# "As this enchantment enters, choose a creature type" is a replacement effect of Arcane Adaptation's own (CR 614.1c,
# 614.12a), and which apply is judged on the permanent "as it would exist on the battlefield, taking into account ...
# continuous effects that already exist and would apply to the permanent" (CR 614.12). With Opalescence and Humility out,
# Arcane Adaptation would be a creature there (Opalescence, layer 4) with no abilities (Humility, layer 6), so nothing is
# chosen as it enters on turn 5 (the refusal "! Bot1.Modes" holds across its resolution) and it has no chosen type. It is a
# 1/1 enchantment creature: Opalescence's 3/3 first, then the later Humility's 1/1 (layer 7b, CR 613.7). On turn 7 Bot1
# disenchants Humility: Arcane Adaptation has its ability again, and is a creature Bot1 controls, but with no type chosen
# it adds none - to itself or anything else - and is Opalescence's 3/3.

